    {
      "id": "kpi_operational_rate",
      "info": "Share of ASSESSED sites whose latest monitoring found them operational.\nThe counts are the Operational Status ring's, unchanged — the same three questions the map colours its pins by: infrastructure_status (RWS), system_status (EPS), station_status (Pump Stations).\nWWTP and WTP are not in the denominator at all: neither form asks a plant-level status question, so dividing by the whole fleet would report a gap in the forms as a fleet of broken plants. See issue #34 G1 decision 1.\nThe card is filled from its own value — green at 90% or above, amber at 75%, red below — rather than a fixed colour that would stay green at any reading.",
      "chart_type": "cross_asset_card",
      "source": "donut_domain",
      "order": 4,
      "col_span": 5,
      "label": "% Operational",
      "display": "percentage",
      "snapshot_ref": "compliance_snapshot",
      "domain_id": "donut_operational_compliance",
      "caption": "{numerator} of {denominator} assessed",
      "status_thresholds": {
        "good": 90,
        "warning": 75
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kpi_compliance_rate",
      "info": "Share of ASSESSED sites meeting the water-quality standard that applies to them — drinking water for WTP, RWS and EPS; effluent for WWTP.\nEvery family is judged by the rule its own dashboard owns and displays, so this headline moves when a threshold there moves. It pools exactly the sites the Drinking Water and Effluent rings below count, which are disjoint: no asset both supplies drinking water and treats effluent.\nPump Stations are absent — neither rule applies to them.\nSites never sampled, and EPS sites whose sample never went to a lab, are not assessed rather than failing: an untested site is a gap in monitoring, not a breach.",
      "chart_type": "cross_asset_card",
      "source": "formula_domains",
      "order": 5,
      "col_span": 5,
      "label": "Compliance Rate",
      "display": "percentage",
      "snapshot_ref": "compliance_snapshot",
      "domain_ids": ["domain_drinking_water", "domain_effluent"],
      "caption": "{numerator} of {denominator} assessed pass",
      "status_thresholds": {
        "good": 90,
        "warning": 75
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kpi_critical_alerts",
      "info": "Assets whose latest monitoring trips at least one red condition for their family.\nThis is the row count of each All Alerts tab, summed — the same definition, the same criteria, one number. Open All Alerts to see which sites and why.\nOne site counts once however many conditions it trips.",
      "chart_type": "cross_asset_card",
      "source": "escalation",
      "order": 6,
      "col_span": 4,
      "label": "Critical Alerts",
      "caption": "assets need attention",
      "status_when_positive": "critical",
